# D-Card API — system and authentication
# See http/README.md for setup. Environment: local.


### Health check (public)
# Liveness for uptime checks and deploys.
# 200 → { "status": "ok" }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Missing or wrong API key → 401 invalid_api_key (checked before any route runs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health
X-API-Key: not-a-real-key

### Provision the caller's D-Card account (any signed-in user)
# Call once after Firebase sign-up. Creates `user_account` (Firebase UID, email, provider).
# 201 → created · 200 → already existed (same account). 401 without a valid token.
# Response: { "id", "firebaseUid", "email", "authProvider": "password|google|apple", "personId", "isAdmin", "emailVerified", "createdAt" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Current account
# 200 → account · 404 not_found before POST /me · 401 without a token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Missing token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Start a web session (web app only)
# Exchanges a Firebase ID token for the httpOnly `dcard_session` cookie (5 days).
# 204 + Set-Cookie. 401 for an invalid token. Apps keep using the bearer header instead.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/session
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "idToken": "{{hostToken}}" }

### End the web session
# 204 + expired cookie.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/session
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Get a Firebase ID token (dev / production)
# Signs in an existing Firebase user (email/password) directly with Firebase — not the D-Card API,
# so no X-API-Key. Copy `idToken` from the response into hostToken (or another *Token) in
# http/http-client.private.env.json for that environment. Tokens expire after 1 hour. Local keeps using fake: tokens.
# 200 → { "idToken", "email", "localId", "expiresIn": "3600", … } · 400 INVALID_LOGIN_CREDENTIALS.
POST https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signInWithPassword?key={{firebaseWebApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{testUserEmail}}", "password": "{{testUserPassword}}", "returnSecureToken": true }

